This level uses find command once again with the similar attributes to search with a little knowledge over the file structure of linux.

HINT: file is somewhere in the system indicates that it is not in the current dir.

so to locate this file we use the command in the following way 

" find / -user bandit7 -group bandit6 -size 33c 2>/dev/null "

/ -> indicates find any file in the entire system with the following attribytes that are specified 
2>/dev/null -> indiacates that if any STDERR(2) is redirected to /dev/null . 
